  world:
    factors:
    - id: government
      question: Who runs 2150?
      answer: 2
      foundAs: 
      statusQuo: directorate
      splitLine: '{a} and {b}, sharing the building'
      splitHeadline: 'TWO GOVERNMENTS: {a} and {b} both claim the Directorate building.
        Each has opened its own queue.'
    - id: future
      question: What does 2150 run on?
      answer: 2
      foundAs: 
      statusQuo: credit_age
      splitLine: '{a} and {b}, one on each bank of the river'
      splitHeadline: '2150 IS SPLIT: {a} on one bank of the river, {b} on the other.
        The bridge is very busy.'
    - id: money
      question: How does 2150 pay its way?
      answer: 2
      foundAs: 
      statusQuo: debt
      splitLine: '{a} and {b}, side by side'
      splitHeadline: 'TWO PURSES: 2150 pays its way through {a} and {b} at once.
        Every till now has two drawers.'
    - id: culture
      question: Whose culture leads?
      answer: 1
      foundAs: 'None: the neutral Temporal Customs Zone'
      statusQuo: 
      splitLine: 
      splitHeadline: 
    outcomes:
    - factor: government
      id: directorate
      name: The Directorate
      headline: 'DIRECTORATE: the Customs Directorate carries on running 2150. The
        queues reopen at nine, as always.'
      report: 'The Customs Directorate runs 2150 as it always has: by form, by queue
        and by stamp. Every citizen knows exactly which counter to stand at.'
    - factor: government
      id: democracy
      name: Democracy
      headline: '2150 VOTES: the Directorate hands the building to an elected assembly.
        Its first sitting ran eleven hours.'
      report: An elected assembly runs 2150 and votes on everything, including the
        colour of the ballot papers. Anyone may stand for office, and nearly everyone
        does.
    - factor: government
      id: monarchy
      name: Monarchy
      headline: 'A CROWN FOR 2150: a monarch is proclaimed on the Directorate steps.
        The queues are now royal queues.'
      report: A monarch reigns over 2150 from a palace that used to be a transit
        hall. Every form carries the royal crest, and people have started framing
        them.
    - factor: government
      id: fascism
      name: Fascism
      headline: 'ORDER: a single party takes charge of 2150. Uniforms are issued,
        and every portal opens to the second.'
      report: One party runs 2150, and one flag hangs over every portal. The timetables
        are exact, the parades are long, and nobody steps out of the queue.
    - factor: government
      id: communism
      name: Communism
      headline: 'THE PEOPLE''S DESK: workers'' councils take over the Directorate.
        Every desk now has a committee.'
      report: Workers' councils run 2150 and hold the portals in common. Every clerk
        is a comrade, every queue is shared equally, and the five-year plan has a
        ten-year appendix.
    - factor: government
      id: theocracy
      name: Theocracy
      headline: 'BY SACRED ORDER: 2150''s temple councils take up the Directorate''s
        duties. The stamps are blessed each morning.'
      report: Temple councils govern 2150, and every departure begins with a blessing
        of the portal. The calendar has many more holidays, and the queues wait in
        respectful silence.
    - factor: government
      id: technocracy
      name: Technocracy
      headline: 'RUN BY EXPERTS: a council of engineers takes over 2150. Its first
        decree is a flowchart.'
      report: Engineers and statisticians run 2150 through committees of specialists.
        Every law comes with footnotes, and every citizen with a user manual.
    - factor: government
      id: corporate_board
      name: The Corporate Board
      headline: 'UNDER NEW MANAGEMENT: a board of directors acquires 2150. Every
        citizen receives a shareholder newsletter.'
      report: A corporate board runs 2150 as a going concern, with quarterly meetings
        open to anyone holding a share. The minutes are glossy, and the annual report
        has a mascot.
    - factor: future
      id: credit_age
      name: The Credit Age
      headline: 'THE CREDIT AGE: wrist comms, queues and the debt grid carry on.
        2150 runs on credit, as before.'
      report: 2150 runs on wrist comms, credit lines and very long queues. Everything
        is on account, and the account is always open.
    - factor: future
      id: nuclear
      name: The Nuclear Age
      headline: 'ATOMS FOR ALL: 2150''s first home reactor goes on sale. Kettles
        now boil in a second.'
      report: '2150 runs on the atom: reactors in the basements and a gentle glow
        on the night shift. Power is too cheap to meter, so nobody meters it.'
    - factor: future
      id: cybernetic
      name: The Cybernetic Age
      headline: 'WIRED: 2150 connects its citizens straight to the city grid. Queue
        numbers now arrive by thought.'
      report: 2150 runs on implants and thinking machines. Its citizens talk to the
        city, and the city answers back, usually politely.
    - factor: future
      id: space_age
      name: The Space Age
      headline: 'LIFT-OFF: the first launch ring opens over the Aegean. The Space
        League is hiring.'
      report: '2150 looks up: launch rings, orbital suburbs and a weekend commute
        to the Moon. The luggage limits are strict; the view is spectacular.'
    - factor: future
      id: naturalism
      name: Naturalism
      headline: 'BACK TO THE LAND: 2150 switched off the grid for a week, and nobody
        switched it back on. Vineyards climb the arcologies.'
      report: '2150 has rewilded itself: gardens in the transit halls, goats on the
        portals and meetings held under trees. Everything grows, and the paperwork
        is composted.'
    - factor: future
      id: anarchy
      name: Anarchy
      headline: 'NOBODY''S PLAN: 2150''s master plans are cancelled by general agreement.
        Every street now runs itself.'
      report: '2150 runs on whatever works that day: self-built districts, street
        assemblies and improvised machines. There is no timetable, and yet things
        arrive.'
    - factor: money
      id: debt
      name: The Debt
      headline: 'THE DEBT HOLDS: every account in 2150 carries over. Interest compounds
        as usual.'
      report: '2150 pays its way on credit: every citizen carries a debt, and every
        debt passes to kin. The ledger has never once lost track of a cent.'
    - factor: money
      id: jubilee
      name: Jubilee
      headline: 'JUBILEE: every debt in 2150 is forgiven at midnight. Collections
        throws a party.'
      report: Every debt in 2150 was forgiven, and the ledgers were shredded into
        confetti. Nobody owes anybody, and the collectors are learning to knit.
    - factor: money
      id: company_towns
      name: Company Towns
      headline: 'COMPANY TOWN: 2150''s employers take over housing, schools and the
        portals. Wages are paid in company scrip.'
      report: '2150''s employers run daily life: company housing, company schools,
        company songs. Payday comes in scrip, and the canteen is very popular.'
    - factor: money
      id: commons
      name: The Commons
      headline: 'SHARE AND SHARE ALIKE: everything in 2150 goes into common stores.
        The first swap market opens in the transit hall.'
      report: '2150 shares what it has: common stores, swap markets and a library
        of tools. Nothing is bought; everything is borrowed and, mostly, returned.'
    - factor: money
      id: banking_houses
      name: The Banking Houses
      headline: 'HOUSES OF CREDIT: the merchant dynasties open their vaults to 2150.
        Every family now has a banker.'
      report: Merchant banking dynasties finance 2150 from marble halls, lending
        by letter and by handshake. The interest is negotiable, and lunch is included.
    roles:
    - archetype: scientist
      factor: future
      pull: 4
    - archetype: diplomat
      factor: government
      pull: 3
    - archetype: soldier
      factor: government
      pull: 3
    - archetype: merchant
      factor: money
      pull: 5
  news:
    debt:
    - Debt Relief Departures reach a record high.
    - 'CLEAR YOUR DEBT: 180 days in the Victorian mills.'
    - 12,000 accounts frozen in default.
    - Premium families book Periclean Athens for the summer.
    - A stranded tourist's family inherits 212,000 cr.
    stranded: 'Stranded: {name}, lost in {place} when an Economy transponder failed.'
    debtReliefCount: 'Citizens who left on Debt Relief yesterday: {count}.'
    returnedAccepted: 'Second time lucky: {name}, turned away on day {day}, stamped
      through on day {back}.'
    returnedDenied: '{name}, turned away on day {day}, tried again on day {back}.
      Turned away twice.'
  mail:
  - id: welcome
    fromDay: 1
    untilDay: 0
    flag: 
    from: Customs Directorate
    subject: Welcome to Desk 3
    body:
    - Welcome to Temporal Customs. Every traveller at your desk wants to depart for
      the past; your desk decides who goes.
    - Check each paper against the Citizen Records and the reference books, log every
      deviation before you deny, and follow the day's directives.
    - Your pay is credited when each shift ends. Your Citizen Account holds your
      statement. Departures are voluntary.
